yond timeout\"\n   458→    expected:\n   459→      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n   460→    traces:\n   461→      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n   462→\n   463→  - name: env_default_lc_all\n   464→    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n   465→    inputs:\n   466→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n   467→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   468→    expected:\n   469→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n   470→    traces:\n   471→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   472→\n   473→  - name: env_override_lc_all\n   474→    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n   475→    inputs:\n   476→      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n   477→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   478→    expected:\n   479→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n   480→    traces:\n   481→      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n   482→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   483→\n   484→  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n   485→    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n   486→    inputs:\n   487→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n   488→      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n   489→    expected:\n   490→      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n   491→    traces:\n   492→      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n   493→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"e4fbaa65-0cbc-4220-8327-46fa150891ef","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel00.0.yaml","content":"id: test-rel00.0\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel00.0 — build lifecycle, cmd/version, pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils\"\nrelease: rel00.0\n\ntraces:\n  - rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n  - prd011-magefiles R1\n  - prd011-magefiles R2\n  - prd011-magefiles R3\n  - prd011-magefiles R4\n  - rel00.0-uc002-format\n  - prd003-format R1\n  - prd003-format R2\n  - prd003-format R3\n  - rel00.0-uc003-sys\n  - prd002-sys R1\n  - prd002-sys R2\n  - prd002-sys R3\n  - prd002-sys R4\n  - rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n  - prd001-testutils R1\n  - prd001-testutils R2\n  - prd001-testutils R3\n  - prd001-testutils R4\n  - prd001-testutils R5\n\npreconditions:\n  - A git repository with at least one tag matching v[0-9]*.\n  - golangci-lint is installed and on PATH.\n  - mage is installed and on PATH.\n  - configuration.yaml exists at the project root with project.binary_dir set to bin.\n\ntest_cases:\n  # --- uc001-magefiles: build lifecycle and version ---\n\n  - name: build_produces_version_binary\n    description: mage build compiles cmd/version to bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/version exists and is executable\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.4\n\n  - name: version_prints_tag\n    description: bin/version prints the latest version tag and exits 0.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_pattern: \"v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.3\n\n  - name: version_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_v_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version -v produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version -v\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_unknown_flag\n    description: bin/version --bogus prints usage to stderr and exits 2.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --bogus\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 2\n      stdout: \"\"\n      stderr_contains: \"usage\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_dev_build\n    description: A build without ldflags prints \"dev\".\n    inputs:\n      command: \"go build -o /tmp/version-dev ./cmd/version && /tmp/version-dev\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"dev\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n\n  - name: lint_passes\n    description: mage lint runs golangci-lint with no warnings.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage lint\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.2\n\n  - name: clean_removes_bin\n    description: mage clean removes the bin/ directory.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/ does not exist\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  - name: clean_idempotent\n    description: mage clean succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage clean && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  # --- uc002-format: pkg/format output formatting ---\n\n  - name: columns_20_entries_80_width\n    description: Columns distributes 20 filenames into a grid fitting 80 columns.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(entries, 80)\"\n      entries: 20 filenames of varying lengths\n    expected:\n      postcondition: each row fits within 80 characters; column count is maximized\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n      - prd003-format R1.4\n\n  - name: columns_empty_input\n    description: Columns returns nil for empty input.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(nil, 80)\"\n    expected:\n      result: nil\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n\n  - name: pad_right\n    description: PadRight pads a string with trailing spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"abc       \"  (abc + 7 spaces)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: pad_left\n    description: PadLeft pads a string with leading spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadLeft(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"       abc\"  (7 spaces + abc)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: display_width_multibyte\n    description: Column width uses rune count, not byte count, for multi-byte strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"café\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"café      \"  (café is 4 runes, padded to 10)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.3\n\n  - name: file_type_color_all_types\n    description: FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI codes for all eight file types.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(mode) for each file type\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      directory: '\"\\033[34m\"'\n      symlink: '\"\\033[36m\"'\n      executable: '\"\\033[32m\"'\n      block_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      char_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      socket: '\"\\033[35m\"'\n      pipe: '\"\\033[33m\"'\n      regular: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.1\n      - prd003-format R2.4\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled\n    description: Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"\\033[0m\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.2\n\n  - name: color_disabled_suppresses_output\n    description: SetColorEnabled(false) causes FileTypeColor and Reset to return empty strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(os.ModeDir) and format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n    expected:\n      file_type_color: '\"\"'\n      reset: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.6\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled_restores_auto\n    description: ResetColorEnabled clears the override and reverts to TTY detection.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ResetColorEnabled() then format.ColorEnabled(pipe)\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true); format.ResetColorEnabled()\"\n    expected:\n      color_enabled_pipe: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.7\n\n  - name: color_enabled_pipe\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for an os.Pipe writer.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(pipeWriter)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: color_enabled_non_file\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for a bytes.Buffer (non-*os.File).\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(&bytes.Buffer{})\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: human_size_binary\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1024-based units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1536, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.5K\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n      - prd003-format R3.3\n\n  - name: human_size_si\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1000-based SI units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1000000, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.0MB\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n\n  - name: human_size_zero\n    description: HumanSize returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(0, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"0\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.4\n\n  # --- uc003-sys: pkg/sys syscall abstractions ---\n\n  - name: terminal_width_pipe\n    description: TerminalWidth returns an error when stdout is a pipe.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.TerminalWidth() with stdout redirected to a pipe\"\n    expected:\n      error: non-nil\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.1\n\n  - name: is_terminal_pipe_fd\n    description: IsTerminal returns false for a pipe file descriptor.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.IsTerminal(pipeFd)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.3\n\n  - name: stat_known_file\n    description: Stat returns correct extended metadata for a known file.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks match stat(1) output\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.1\n      - prd002-sys R2.2\n\n  - name: lstat_symlink\n    description: Lstat on a symlink returns symlink type bits, not target's mode.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Lstat(symlinkPath)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"Mode & os.ModeSymlink != 0\"\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.1\n\n  - name: stat_modtime_populated\n    description: Stat returns a non-zero ModTime from the platform-correct field.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: ModTime is non-zero and close to os.Stat(testFile).ModTime()\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.3\n\n  - name: stat_hard_link_count\n    description: Stat returns correct Nlink for a file with multiple hard links.\n    inputs:\n      setup: \"create testFile, create hard link to testFile\"\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: Nlink == 2\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.2\n\n  - name: sigpipe_handler_exit_zero\n    description: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() then write to closed pipe\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R3.1\n\n  - name: on_terminal_resize_callback\n    description: OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked on SIGWINCH.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.OnTerminalResize(callback) then send SIGWINCH\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: callback was called with a positive width\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R4.1\n      - prd002-sys R4.2\n\n  - name: cross_platform_compile\n    description: All pkg/sys code compiles on darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 go build ./pkg/sys/ && GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./pkg/sys/\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.2\n\n  # --- uc004-testutils: pkg/testutils differential testing harness ---\n\n  - name: difftest_zero_value\n    description: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, echoBin, echoBin, []DiffTest{{Name: \\\"zero\\\"}})\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R1.1\n\n  - name: rundifftests_matching_output\n    description: RunDiffTests passes silently when both binaries produce identical output.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"both mock binaries print \\\"hello\\\\n\\\" to stdout and exit 0\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output to stdout or stderr\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.1\n      - prd001-testutils R2.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_stdout\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when stdout differs between binaries.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary prints \\\"hello\\\\n\\\", reference prints \\\"world\\\\n\\\"\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"test fails with message containing args, stdin, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_exit_code\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when exit codes differ.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary exits 0, reference exits 1\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing both exit codes\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: timestamp_normalizer\n    description: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so time-dependent outputs match.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Normalize: []NormalizeFunc{TimestampNormalizer}\"\n      setup: \"binaries produce outputs differing only in timestamp field\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes after normalization strips timestamps\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.1\n      - prd001-testutils R4.2\n\n  - name: compose_normalizers\n    description: ComposeNormalizers chains multiple functions applied in order.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.ComposeNormalizers(fn1, fn2)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"composed function applies fn1 then fn2; output matches fn2(fn1(input))\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.3\n      - prd001-testutils R4.4\n\n  - name: expected_files_match\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison passes when Go binary writes correct file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes expected content to output file\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: expected_files_diverge\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison fails when Go binary writes wrong file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes different content than expected\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing file path, expected content, actual content\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: timeout_exceeded\n    description: RunDiffTests fails with timeout message when binary exceeds timeout.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with short timeout\"\n      setup: \"mock binary sleeps beyond timeout\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n\n  - name: env_default_lc_all\n    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n\n  - name: env_override_lc_all\n    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n\n  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n","numLines":493,"startLine":1,"totalLines":493}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CGGyJYQhXgKFrbL4Z8FX9b","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     2→// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     3→\n     4→package sys\n     5→\n     6→import (\n     7→\t\"fmt\"\n     8→\t\"os\"\n     9→\t\"time\"\n    10→\n    11→\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    12→)\n    13→\n    14→// FileInfo holds extended file metadata from the underlying unix.Stat_t,\n    15→// exposing fields not available from os.FileInfo: hard-link count, device\n    16→// and inode numbers, physical block counts, and nanosecond-precision\n    17→// modification time. The struct abstracts Darwin/Linux divergence in Stat_t\n    18→// field names and types so callers use a single API regardless of platform.\n    19→//\n    20→// prd002-sys R2.2.\n    21→type FileInfo struct {\n    22→\tMode    os.FileMode // file mode and type bits (from syscall.Stat_t.Mode)\n    23→\tSize    int64       // apparent file size in bytes (st_size)\n    24→\tNlink   uint64      // hard-link count (st_nlink)\n    25→\tUid     uint32      // owner user ID (st_uid)\n    26→\tGid     uint32      // owner group ID (st_gid)\n    27→\tRdev    uint64      // device ID for special files (st_rdev)\n    28→\tDev     uint64      // device ID of the containing filesystem (st_dev)\n    29→\tIno     uint64      // inode number (st_ino)\n    30→\tBlocks  int64       // number of 512-byte blocks allocated (st_blocks)\n    31→\tBlksize int64       // preferred I/O block size (st_blksize)\n    32→\tModTime time.Time   // modification time (st_mtime / st_mtimespec)\n    33→\tInfo    os.FileInfo // underlying os.FileInfo for os package compatibility\n    34→}\n    35→\n    36→// Stat returns extended file metadata for path, following symbolic links.\n    37→// It combines os.Stat (for os.FileInfo compatibility) with unix.Stat (for\n    38→// extended Stat_t fields). Platform-divergent field extraction is handled\n    39→// by fillFromStat in stat_darwin.go / stat_linux.go.\n    40→//\n    41→// prd002-sys R2.1.\n    42→func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) {\n    43→\tvar st unix.Stat_t\n    44→\tif err := unix.Stat(path, &st); err != nil {\n    45→\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"stat %s: %w\", path, err)\n    46→\t}\n    47→\tosInfo, err := os.Stat(path)\n    48→\tif err != nil {\n    49→\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"stat %s: %w\", path, err)\n    50→\t}\n    51→\treturn newFileInfo(&st, osInfo), nil\n    52→}\n    53→\n    54→// Lstat returns extended file metadata for path without following symbolic\n    55→// links. When path is a symlink, the returned FileInfo describes the symlink\n    56→// itself, not its target.\n    57→//\n    58→// prd002-sys R2.1.\n    59→func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) {\n    60→\tvar st unix.Stat_t\n    61→\tif err := unix.Lstat(path, &st); err != nil {\n    62→\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"lstat %s: %w\", path, err)\n    63→\t}\n    64→\tosInfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n    65→\tif err != nil {\n    66→\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"lstat %s: %w\", path, err)\n    67→\t}\n    68→\treturn newFileInfo(&st, osInfo), nil\n    69→}\n    70→\n    71→// newFileInfo populates a FileInfo from a unix.Stat_t and the corresponding\n    72→// os.FileInfo. Fields with identical types across Darwin and Linux are set\n    73→// here. Platform-divergent fields (ModTime, Nlink, Dev, Rdev, Blksize) are\n    74→// populated by fillFromStat, defined in stat_darwin.go and stat_linux.go.\n    75→//\n    76→// prd002-sys R2.2, R2.3.\n    77→func newFileInfo(st *unix.Stat_t, osInfo os.FileInfo) *FileInfo {\n    78→\tfi := &FileInfo{\n    79→\t\tMode:   osInfo.Mode(),\n    80→\t\tSize:   st.Size,\n    81→\t\tUid:    st.Uid,\n    82→\t\tGid:    st.Gid,\n    83→\t\tIno:    st.Ino,\n    84→\t\tBlocks: st.Blocks,\n    85→\t\tInfo:   osInfo,\n    86→\t}\n    87→\tfillFromStat(fi, st)\n    88→\treturn fi\n    89→}\n    90→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"709cdf99-48a7-4074-a154-bfe8b3e35a58","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/pkg/sys/stat.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n)\n\n// FileInfo holds extended file metadata from the underlying unix.Stat_t,\n// exposing fields not available from os.FileInfo: hard-link count, device\n// and inode numbers, physical block counts, and nanosecond-precision\n// modification time. The struct abstracts Darwin/Linux divergence in Stat_t\n// field names and types so callers use a single API regardless of platform.\n//\n// prd002-sys R2.2.\ntype FileInfo struct {\n\tMode    os.FileMode // file mode and type bits (from syscall.Stat_t.Mode)\n\tSize    int64       // apparent file size in bytes (st_size)\n\tNlink   uint64      // hard-link count (st_nlink)\n\tUid     uint32      // owner user ID (st_uid)\n\tGid     uint32      // owner group ID (st_gid)\n\tRdev    uint64      // device ID for special files (st_rdev)\n\tDev     uint64      // device ID of the containing filesystem (st_dev)\n\tIno     uint64      // inode number (st_ino)\n\tBlocks  int64       // number of 512-byte blocks allocated (st_blocks)\n\tBlksize int64       // preferred I/O block size (st_blksize)\n\tModTime time.Time   // modification time (st_mtime / st_mtimespec)\n\tInfo    os.FileInfo // underlying os.FileInfo for os package compatibility\n}\n\n// Stat returns extended file metadata for path, following symbolic links.\n// It combines os.Stat (for os.FileInfo compatibility) with unix.Stat (for\n// extended Stat_t fields). Platform-divergent field extraction is handled\n// by fillFromStat in stat_darwin.go / stat_linux.go.\n//\n// prd002-sys R2.1.\nfunc Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) {\n\tvar st unix.Stat_t\n\tif err := unix.Stat(path, &st); err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"stat %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\tosInfo, err := os.Stat(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"stat %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\treturn newFileInfo(&st, osInfo), nil\n}\n\n// Lstat returns extended file metadata for path without following symbolic\n// links. When path is a symlink, the returned FileInfo describes the symlink\n// itself, not its target.\n//\n// prd002-sys R2.1.\nfunc Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) {\n\tvar st unix.Stat_t\n\tif err := unix.Lstat(path, &st); err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"lstat %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\tosInfo, err := os.Lstat(path)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"lstat %s: %w\", path, err)\n\t}\n\treturn newFileInfo(&st, osInfo), nil\n}\n\n// newFileInfo populates a FileInfo from a unix.Stat_t and the corresponding\n// os.FileInfo. Fields with identical types across Darwin and Linux are set\n// here. Platform-divergent fields (ModTime, Nlink, Dev, Rdev, Blksize) are\n// populated by fillFromStat, defined in stat_darwin.go and stat_linux.go.\n//\n// prd002-sys R2.2, R2.3.\nfunc newFileInfo(st *unix.Stat_t, osInfo os.FileInfo) *FileInfo {\n\tfi := &FileInfo{\n\t\tMode:   osInfo.Mode(),\n\t\tSize:   st.Size,\n\t\tUid:    st.Uid,\n\t\tGid:    st.Gid,\n\t\tIno:    st.Ino,\n\t\tBlocks: st.Blocks,\n\t\tInfo:   osInfo,\n\t}\n\tfillFromStat(fi, st)\n\treturn fi\n}\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BJQDCoJQCmi6tkRBgnXx7N","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd002-sys\n     2→title: \"pkg/sys: Syscall Abstractions\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  Four utilities (ls, du, find, xargs) need OS-level capabilities that Go's standard\n     6→  library does not expose in a portable, stable form: terminal-width queries, extended\n     7→  file metadata (hard-link count, device and inode numbers, physical block counts),\n     8→  and signal handling for SIGPIPE and SIGWINCH. On Darwin and Linux these syscalls\n     9→  diverge in struct layout (st_mtimespec vs st_mtim, st_blocks interpretation) and\n    10→  available interfaces (TIOCGWINSZ ioctl). Without pkg/sys each cmd/ package would\n    11→  import syscall or golang.org/x/sys directly, duplicating the Darwin/Linux divergence\n    12→  handling and making it harder to test or audit the syscall surface.\n    13→\n    14→  pkg/sys provides a stable, tested interface for these three capability areas. Each\n    15→  capability is driven by at least one concrete utility requirement derived from C source\n    16→  analysis (see dependency-map.yaml).\n    17→\n    18→goals:\n    19→  - G1: Provide a portable terminal-width query that works on Darwin and Linux without cgo.\n    20→  - G2: Expose extended file metadata (st_nlink, st_uid, st_gid, st_rdev, st_blocks, st_ino, st_dev) not available from os.FileInfo.\n    21→  - G3: Provide a SIGPIPE handler that suppresses the broken-pipe error when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer.\n    22→  - G4: Provide a SIGWINCH handler that calls a user-supplied callback when the terminal is resized.\n    23→\n    24→requirements:\n    25→  R1:\n    26→    title: Terminal width and TTY detection\n    27→    items:\n    28→      - R1.1: Must provide func TerminalWidth() (int, error) that returns the current terminal column count by calling ioctl(TIOCGWINSZ) on stdout. Returns an error (not panic) when stdout is not a terminal or when ioctl fails.\n    29→      - R1.2: Must use golang.org/x/sys/unix (the project's only external dependency) to perform the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl; must not shell out to tput or stty and must not import golang.org/x/term.\n    30→      - R1.3: |\n    31→          Must provide func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool that returns true when the file\n    32→          descriptor refers to a terminal, and false otherwise. Implementation: call\n    33→          golang.org/x/sys/unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ) and return\n    34→          err == nil. Returns false for pipes, regular files, and non-terminal descriptors.\n    35→          The caller (pkg/format ColorEnabled) is responsible for extracting the fd from an\n    36→          io.Writer via type assertion to *os.File. Required by pkg/format to suppress color\n    37→          output when stdout is redirected.\n    38→      - R1.4: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281): ls uses struct winsize to determine column count for its default multi-column layout and for the -w/--width flag default.'\n    39→\n    40→  R2:\n    41→    title: Extended file metadata\n    42→    items:\n    43→      - R2.1: Must provide func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error). Stat follows symbolic links (equivalent to os.Stat); Lstat does not follow symbolic links (equivalent to os.Lstat). Both return a *FileInfo populated from syscall.Stat_t.\n    44→      - R2.2: |\n    45→          FileInfo must be defined as the following named struct in package sys:\n    46→\n    47→            type FileInfo struct {\n    48→                Mode    os.FileMode // file mode and type bits (from syscall.Stat_t.Mode)\n    49→                Size    int64       // apparent file size in bytes (st_size)\n    50→                Nlink   uint64      // hard-link count (st_nlink)\n    51→                Uid     uint32      // owner user ID (st_uid)\n    52→                Gid     uint32      // owner group ID (st_gid)\n    53→                Rdev    uint64      // device ID for special files (st_rdev)\n    54→                Dev     uint64      // device ID of the containing filesystem (st_dev)\n    55→                Ino     uint64      // inode number (st_ino)\n    56→                Blocks  int64       // number of 512-byte blocks allocated (st_blocks)\n    57→                Blksize int64       // preferred I/O block size (st_blksize)\n    58→                ModTime time.Time   // modification time (st_mtime / st_mtimespec)\n    59→                Info    os.FileInfo // underlying os.FileInfo for os package compatibility\n    60→            }\n    61→      - R2.3: Must abstract the Darwin/Linux divergence in struct field names (st_mtimespec on Darwin vs st_mtim on Linux; st_blocks interpretation) so callers use a single API regardless of target platform.\n    62→      - R2.4: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:213, 371): ls needs Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Mode for -l format; Blocks for -s; Ino for -i.'\n    63→      - R2.5: 'Utility context — du (du.c:554): du needs Dev and Ino for hard-link deduplication, and Blocks for physical block-count accumulation.'\n    64→      - R2.6: 'Utility context — find (find/ftsfind.c:172): find predicates (-type, -size, -newer, -perm, -uid, -gid) require Mode, Size, ModTime, Uid, Gid, Nlink from the stat struct.'\n    65→\n    66→  R3:\n    67→    title: SIGPIPE handling\n    68→    items:\n    69→      - R3.1: |\n    70→          Must provide func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() that installs a SIGPIPE handler causing the process to exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer. Implementation: use signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE) with a buffered channel of size 1; in a dedicated goroutine call os.Exit(0) when the channel receives. Must not use signal.Ignore so that deferred cleanup functions do not run on SIGPIPE (matching GNU behavior where SIGPIPE terminates silently).\n    71→      - R3.2: InstallSIGPIPEHandler must be safe to call multiple times; only one goroutine per invocation is started.\n    72→      - R3.3: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:1600-1620): ls installs a SIGPIPE handler via sigaction so that piping ls output to head does not produce a broken-pipe error message. du, find, and xargs have the same requirement.'\n    73→\n    74→  R4:\n    75→    title: SIGWINCH handling\n    76→    items:\n    77→      - R4.1: |\n    78→          Must provide func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) that registers a SIGWINCH handler. When the terminal is resized, the handler calls TerminalWidth() and invokes the callback with the new width. If TerminalWidth() returns an error the callback is not invoked.\n    79→      - R4.2: Must support multiple calls to OnTerminalResize; each registered callback must be called on resize. Callbacks are called in registration order.\n    80→      - R4.3: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281, SIGWINCH registration): ls re-queries terminal width on SIGWINCH to re-format output when the terminal window is resized during a long listing.'\n    81→\n    82→non_goals:\n    83→  - pkg/sys does not wrap all of syscall or golang.org/x/sys; it exposes only the surfaces required by the current utility batch.\n    84→  - pkg/sys does not provide file-watching or inotify/kqueue interfaces.\n    85→  - pkg/sys does not handle SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 (find's debug output); those are deferred to the find PRD.\n    86→  - pkg/sys does not provide process-group or terminal control (TIOCGPGRP, tcsetpgrp); those are deferred to the xargs PRD.\n    87→\n    88→acceptance_criteria:\n    89→  - \"AC1: TerminalWidth() returns a positive integer when called in a test with a pseudo-terminal (golang.org/x/term's test helpers or os.Pipe() as a TTY substitute is acceptable).\"\n    90→  - \"AC2: Stat() and Lstat() on a known file return FileInfo with correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, and Blocks values as confirmed by running stat(1) on the same file.\"\n    91→  - \"AC3: Lstat() on a symlink returns the symlink's own st_mode (type bits show symlink), not the target's mode.\"\n    92→  - \"AC4: InstallSIGPIPEHandler() causes a process writing to a broken pipe to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\"\n    93→  - \"AC5: All pkg/sys code compiles on both darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 with no build errors and no cgo.\"\n    94→  - \"AC6: All pkg/sys code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    95→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"08bcd623-5262-499d-8223-a4604cb0eecc","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml","content":"id: prd002-sys\ntitle: \"pkg/sys: Syscall Abstractions\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Four utilities (ls, du, find, xargs) need OS-level capabilities that Go's standard\n  library does not expose in a portable, stable form: terminal-width queries, extended\n  file metadata (hard-link count, device and inode numbers, physical block counts),\n  and signal handling for SIGPIPE and SIGWINCH. On Darwin and Linux these syscalls\n  diverge in struct layout (st_mtimespec vs st_mtim, st_blocks interpretation) and\n  available interfaces (TIOCGWINSZ ioctl). Without pkg/sys each cmd/ package would\n  import syscall or golang.org/x/sys directly, duplicating the Darwin/Linux divergence\n  handling and making it harder to test or audit the syscall surface.\n\n  pkg/sys provides a stable, tested interface for these three capability areas. Each\n  capability is driven by at least one concrete utility requirement derived from C source\n  analysis (see dependency-map.yaml).\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Provide a portable terminal-width query that works on Darwin and Linux without cgo.\n  - G2: Expose extended file metadata (st_nlink, st_uid, st_gid, st_rdev, st_blocks, st_ino, st_dev) not available from os.FileInfo.\n  - G3: Provide a SIGPIPE handler that suppresses the broken-pipe error when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer.\n  - G4: Provide a SIGWINCH handler that calls a user-supplied callback when the terminal is resized.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Terminal width and TTY detection\n    items:\n      - R1.1: Must provide func TerminalWidth() (int, error) that returns the current terminal column count by calling ioctl(TIOCGWINSZ) on stdout. Returns an error (not panic) when stdout is not a terminal or when ioctl fails.\n      - R1.2: Must use golang.org/x/sys/unix (the project's only external dependency) to perform the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl; must not shell out to tput or stty and must not import golang.org/x/term.\n      - R1.3: |\n          Must provide func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool that returns true when the file\n          descriptor refers to a terminal, and false otherwise. Implementation: call\n          golang.org/x/sys/unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ) and return\n          err == nil. Returns false for pipes, regular files, and non-terminal descriptors.\n          The caller (pkg/format ColorEnabled) is responsible for extracting the fd from an\n          io.Writer via type assertion to *os.File. Required by pkg/format to suppress color\n          output when stdout is redirected.\n      - R1.4: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281): ls uses struct winsize to determine column count for its default multi-column layout and for the -w/--width flag default.'\n\n  R2:\n    title: Extended file metadata\n    items:\n      - R2.1: Must provide func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error). Stat follows symbolic links (equivalent to os.Stat); Lstat does not follow symbolic links (equivalent to os.Lstat). Both return a *FileInfo populated from syscall.Stat_t.\n      - R2.2: |\n          FileInfo must be defined as the following named struct in package sys:\n\n            type FileInfo struct {\n                Mode    os.FileMode // file mode and type bits (from syscall.Stat_t.Mode)\n                Size    int64       // apparent file size in bytes (st_size)\n                Nlink   uint64      // hard-link count (st_nlink)\n                Uid     uint32      // owner user ID (st_uid)\n                Gid     uint32      // owner group ID (st_gid)\n                Rdev    uint64      // device ID for special files (st_rdev)\n                Dev     uint64      // device ID of the containing filesystem (st_dev)\n                Ino     uint64      // inode number (st_ino)\n                Blocks  int64       // number of 512-byte blocks allocated (st_blocks)\n                Blksize int64       // preferred I/O block size (st_blksize)\n                ModTime time.Time   // modification time (st_mtime / st_mtimespec)\n                Info    os.FileInfo // underlying os.FileInfo for os package compatibility\n            }\n      - R2.3: Must abstract the Darwin/Linux divergence in struct field names (st_mtimespec on Darwin vs st_mtim on Linux; st_blocks interpretation) so callers use a single API regardless of target platform.\n      - R2.4: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:213, 371): ls needs Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Mode for -l format; Blocks for -s; Ino for -i.'\n      - R2.5: 'Utility context — du (du.c:554): du needs Dev and Ino for hard-link deduplication, and Blocks for physical block-count accumulation.'\n      - R2.6: 'Utility context — find (find/ftsfind.c:172): find predicates (-type, -size, -newer, -perm, -uid, -gid) require Mode, Size, ModTime, Uid, Gid, Nlink from the stat struct.'\n\n  R3:\n    title: SIGPIPE handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1: |\n          Must provide func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() that installs a SIGPIPE handler causing the process to exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer. Implementation: use signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE) with a buffered channel of size 1; in a dedicated goroutine call os.Exit(0) when the channel receives. Must not use signal.Ignore so that deferred cleanup functions do not run on SIGPIPE (matching GNU behavior where SIGPIPE terminates silently).\n      - R3.2: InstallSIGPIPEHandler must be safe to call multiple times; only one goroutine per invocation is started.\n      - R3.3: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:1600-1620): ls installs a SIGPIPE handler via sigaction so that piping ls output to head does not produce a broken-pipe error message. du, find, and xargs have the same requirement.'\n\n  R4:\n    title: SIGWINCH handling\n    items:\n      - R4.1: |\n          Must provide func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) that registers a SIGWINCH handler. When the terminal is resized, the handler calls TerminalWidth() and invokes the callback with the new width. If TerminalWidth() returns an error the callback is not invoked.\n      - R4.2: Must support multiple calls to OnTerminalResize; each registered callback must be called on resize. Callbacks are called in registration order.\n      - R4.3: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281, SIGWINCH registration): ls re-queries terminal width on SIGWINCH to re-format output when the terminal window is resized during a long listing.'\n\nnon_goals:\n  - pkg/sys does not wrap all of syscall or golang.org/x/sys; it exposes only the surfaces required by the current utility batch.\n  - pkg/sys does not provide file-watching or inotify/kqueue interfaces.\n  - pkg/sys does not handle SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 (find's debug output); those are deferred to the find PRD.\n  - pkg/sys does not provide process-group or terminal control (TIOCGPGRP, tcsetpgrp); those are deferred to the xargs PRD.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: TerminalWidth() returns a positive integer when called in a test with a pseudo-terminal (golang.org/x/term's test helpers or os.Pipe() as a TTY substitute is acceptable).\"\n  - \"AC2: Stat() and Lstat() on a known file return FileInfo with correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, and Blocks values as confirmed by running stat(1) on the same file.\"\n  - \"AC3: Lstat() on a symlink returns the symlink's own st_mode (type bits show symlink), not the target's mode.\"\n  - \"AC4: InstallSIGPIPEHandler() causes a process writing to a broken pipe to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\"\n  - \"AC5: All pkg/sys code compiles on both darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 with no build errors and no cgo.\"\n  - \"AC6: All pkg/sys code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AXnWF8k516nYnPF6EXEuHL","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc003-sys\n     2→title: \"Query terminal width, stat files, and handle signals via pkg/sys\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator verifies that pkg/sys provides correct terminal-width queries, extended\n     6→  file metadata, and signal handling on both Darwin and Linux. The test exercises each\n     7→  capability in isolation: TerminalWidth returns a positive column count on a TTY,\n     8→  IsTerminal distinguishes terminals from pipes, Stat and Lstat return correct extended\n     9→  metadata, InstallSIGPIPEHandler suppresses broken-pipe errors, and OnTerminalResize\n    10→  invokes callbacks on SIGWINCH.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd002-sys.yaml) and wants to verify that\n    16→  pkg/sys satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs go test ./pkg/sys/... which executes the unit tests for pkg/sys.\n    22→      Unlike cmd/ packages, pkg/sys does not use differential testing because there is no\n    23→      reference binary — it is a library.\n    24→  - id: F2\n    25→    step: |\n    26→      The TerminalWidth test calls TerminalWidth() and verifies it returns a positive\n    27→      integer when stdout is a terminal, or an error when stdout is a pipe.\n    28→  - id: F3\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      The IsTerminal test calls IsTerminal with a pipe fd and verifies it returns false.\n    31→      It calls IsTerminal with a TTY fd (if available in the test environment) and verifies\n    32→      it returns true.\n    33→  - id: F4\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The Stat test calls Stat on a known file and verifies Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino,\n    36→      and Blocks match the output of stat(1) on the same file.\n    37→  - id: F5\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The Lstat test calls Lstat on a symbolic link and verifies that the returned FileInfo\n    40→      has type bits showing symlink, not the target's mode.\n    41→  - id: F6\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The fillFromStat test verifies that the Darwin/Linux abstraction correctly populates\n    44→      FileInfo.ModTime from st_mtimespec (Darwin) or st_mtim (Linux).\n    45→  - id: F7\n    46→    step: |\n    47→      The InstallSIGPIPEHandler test verifies that writing to a broken pipe after installing\n    48→      the handler causes the process to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\n    49→\n    50→touchpoints:\n    51→  - T1: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, IsTerminal (prd002-sys R1)\"\n    52→  - T2: \"pkg/sys — Stat, Lstat, FileInfo, fillFromStat (prd002-sys R2)\"\n    53→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler (prd002-sys R3)\"\n    54→  - T4: \"pkg/sys — OnTerminalResize (prd002-sys R4)\"\n    55→\n    56→success_criteria:\n    57→  - id: S1\n    58→    criterion: TerminalWidth returns a positive integer on a TTY or an error on a pipe.\n    59→  - id: S2\n    60→    criterion: IsTerminal(pipeFd) returns false.\n    61→  - id: S3\n    62→    criterion: Stat on a known file returns correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks.\n    63→  - id: S4\n    64→    criterion: Lstat on a symlink returns type bits showing symlink.\n    65→  - id: S5\n    66→    criterion: FileInfo.ModTime is populated from the platform-correct field.\n    67→  - id: S6\n    68→    criterion: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n    69→  - id: S7\n    70→    criterion: go test ./pkg/sys/... passes on darwin/arm64 with no failures.\n    71→\n    72→out_of_scope:\n    73→  - SIGWINCH testing requires a real terminal resize event; it is tested manually, not in the harness.\n    74→  - Process-group management (setpgid, killpg) is deferred to the xargs PRD.\n    75→  - SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 handling is deferred to the find PRD.\n    76→\n    77→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    78→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"6e6bd619-9b92-4a57-bc6e-19b4b228821e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc003-sys\ntitle: \"Query terminal width, stat files, and handle signals via pkg/sys\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator verifies that pkg/sys provides correct terminal-width queries, extended\n  file metadata, and signal handling on both Darwin and Linux. The test exercises each\n  capability in isolation: TerminalWidth returns a positive column count on a TTY,\n  IsTerminal distinguishes terminals from pipes, Stat and Lstat return correct extended\n  metadata, InstallSIGPIPEHandler suppresses broken-pipe errors, and OnTerminalResize\n  invokes callbacks on SIGWINCH.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd002-sys.yaml) and wants to verify that\n  pkg/sys satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs go test ./pkg/sys/... which executes the unit tests for pkg/sys.\n      Unlike cmd/ packages, pkg/sys does not use differential testing because there is no\n      reference binary — it is a library.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The TerminalWidth test calls TerminalWidth() and verifies it returns a positive\n      integer when stdout is a terminal, or an error when stdout is a pipe.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The IsTerminal test calls IsTerminal with a pipe fd and verifies it returns false.\n      It calls IsTerminal with a TTY fd (if available in the test environment) and verifies\n      it returns true.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The Stat test calls Stat on a known file and verifies Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino,\n      and Blocks match the output of stat(1) on the same file.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The Lstat test calls Lstat on a symbolic link and verifies that the returned FileInfo\n      has type bits showing symlink, not the target's mode.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The fillFromStat test verifies that the Darwin/Linux abstraction correctly populates\n      FileInfo.ModTime from st_mtimespec (Darwin) or st_mtim (Linux).\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The InstallSIGPIPEHandler test verifies that writing to a broken pipe after installing\n      the handler causes the process to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, IsTerminal (prd002-sys R1)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/sys — Stat, Lstat, FileInfo, fillFromStat (prd002-sys R2)\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler (prd002-sys R3)\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/sys — OnTerminalResize (prd002-sys R4)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: TerminalWidth returns a positive integer on a TTY or an error on a pipe.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: IsTerminal(pipeFd) returns false.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: Stat on a known file returns correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: Lstat on a symlink returns type bits showing symlink.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: FileInfo.ModTime is populated from the platform-correct field.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: go test ./pkg/sys/... passes on darwin/arm64 with no failures.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - SIGWINCH testing requires a real terminal resize event; it is tested manually, not in the harness.\n  - Process-group management (setpgid, killpg) is deferred to the xargs PRD.\n  - SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 handling is deferred to the find PRD.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dg3x4cQiWtADbt4p8VovQ7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     2→// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     3→\n     4→// Package sys wraps Darwin and Linux syscalls, providing a stable interface\n     5→// for cmd/ packages. Only syscalls that have platform divergence between\n     6→// Darwin and Linux, or that Go's standard library does not expose cleanly,\n     7→// belong here. cmd/ packages use pkg/sys instead of importing\n     8→// golang.org/x/sys/unix directly.\n     9→//\n    10→// Implements prd002-sys (R1, R2).\n    11→package sys\n    12→\n    13→import (\n    14→\t\"fmt\"\n    15→\n    16→\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    17→)\n    18→\n    19→// IsTerminal reports whether fd refers to a terminal device. It calls the\n    20→// TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via golang.org/x/sys/unix and returns true when the call\n    21→// succeeds. Returns false for pipes, regular files, and other non-terminal\n    22→// descriptors.\n    23→//\n    24→// prd002-sys R1.3.\n    25→func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool {\n    26→\t_, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n    27→\treturn err == nil\n    28→}\n    29→\n    30→// TerminalSize queries the terminal dimensions (rows and columns) for the given\n    31→// file descriptor using the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via golang.org/x/sys/unix.\n    32→// Returns an error when fd is not a terminal or the ioctl fails.\n    33→//\n    34→// prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2.\n    35→func TerminalSize(fd uintptr) (rows int, cols int, err error) {\n    36→\tws, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n    37→\tif err != nil {\n    38→\t\treturn 0, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"querying terminal size: %w\", err)\n    39→\t}\n    40→\treturn int(ws.Row), int(ws.Col), nil\n    41→}\n    42→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"cde88c3d-3096-4444-9f49-5bc426eaec20","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/pkg/sys/terminal.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Package sys wraps Darwin and Linux syscalls, providing a stable interface\n// for cmd/ packages. Only syscalls that have platform divergence between\n// Darwin and Linux, or that Go's standard library does not expose cleanly,\n// belong here. cmd/ packages use pkg/sys instead of importing\n// golang.org/x/sys/unix directly.\n//\n// Implements prd002-sys (R1, R2).\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\n\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n)\n\n// IsTerminal reports whether fd refers to a terminal device. It calls the\n// TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via golang.org/x/sys/unix and returns true when the call\n// succeeds. Returns false for pipes, regular files, and other non-terminal\n// descriptors.\n//\n// prd002-sys R1.3.\nfunc IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool {\n\t_, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n\treturn err == nil\n}\n\n// TerminalSize queries the terminal dimensions (rows and columns) for the given\n// file descriptor using the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl via golang.org/x/sys/unix.\n// Returns an error when fd is not a terminal or the ioctl fails.\n//\n// prd002-sys R1.1, R1.2.\nfunc TerminalSize(fd uintptr) (rows int, cols int, err error) {\n\tws, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, 0, fmt.Errorf(\"querying terminal size: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn int(ws.Row), int(ws.Col), nil\n}\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011iFEwqL98uG4D3W6d3ax3M","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     2→// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     3→\n     4→//go:build darwin\n     5→\n     6→package sys\n     7→\n     8→import (\n     9→\t\"time\"\n    10→\n    11→\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    12→)\n    13→\n    14→// fillFromStat populates the platform-divergent fields of FileInfo from a\n    15→// Darwin unix.Stat_t. Darwin uses Mtimespec (not Mtim) for modification time,\n    16→// uint16 for Nlink, int32 for Dev/Rdev, and int32 for Blksize.\n    17→//\n    18→// prd002-sys R2.3.\n    19→func fillFromStat(fi *FileInfo, st *unix.Stat_t) {\n    20→\tfi.ModTime = time.Unix(st.Mtimespec.Sec, st.Mtimespec.Nsec)\n    21→\tfi.Nlink = uint64(st.Nlink)\n    22→\tfi.Dev = uint64(st.Dev)\n    23→\tfi.Rdev = uint64(st.Rdev)\n    24→\tfi.Blksize = int64(st.Blksize)\n    25→}\n    26→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"755d4b4d-4c87-4aab-aa30-62e63c95408c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n//go:build darwin\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n)\n\n// fillFromStat populates the platform-divergent fields of FileInfo from a\n// Darwin unix.Stat_t. Darwin uses Mtimespec (not Mtim) for modification time,\n// uint16 for Nlink, int32 for Dev/Rdev, and int32 for Blksize.\n//\n// prd002-sys R2.3.\nfunc fillFromStat(fi *FileInfo, st *unix.Stat_t) {\n\tfi.ModTime = time.Unix(st.Mtimespec.Sec, st.Mtimespec.Nsec)\n\tfi.Nlink = uint64(st.Nlink)\n\tfi.Dev = uint64(st.Dev)\n\tfi.Rdev = uint64(st.Rdev)\n\tfi.Blksize = int64(st.Blksize)\n}\n","numLines":26,"startLine":1,"totalLines":26}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QfGm73Gj8cPuYu1uNN9Tif","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     2→// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     3→\n     4→//go:build linux\n     5→\n     6→package sys\n     7→\n     8→import (\n     9→\t\"time\"\n    10→\n    11→\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    12→)\n    13→\n    14→// fillFromStat populates the platform-divergent fields of FileInfo from a\n    15→// Linux unix.Stat_t. Linux uses Mtim (not Mtimespec) for modification time.\n    16→// Field widths vary by architecture (e.g., Nlink is uint32 on arm64, uint64\n    17→// on amd64), so explicit conversions are used for portability.\n    18→//\n    19→// prd002-sys R2.3.\n    20→func fillFromStat(fi *FileInfo, st *unix.Stat_t) {\n    21→\tfi.ModTime = time.Unix(st.Mtim.Sec, st.Mtim.Nsec)\n    22→\tfi.Nlink = uint64(st.Nlink)\n    23→\tfi.Dev = st.Dev\n    24→\tfi.Rdev = st.Rdev\n    25→\tfi.Blksize = int64(st.Blksize)\n    26→}\n    27→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3fb5a884-dc99-4051-9107-9e94fb33ddd1","uuid":"7e582f7d-7e57-44d7-8506-f11591fa6419","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/127/pkg/sys/stat_linux.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n//go:build linux\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n)\n\n// fillFromStat populates the platform-divergent fields of FileInfo from a\n// Linux unix.Stat_t. Linux uses Mtim (not Mtimespec) for modification time.\n// Field widths vary by architecture (e.g., Nlink is uint32 on arm64, uint64\n// on amd64), so explicit conversions are used for portability.\n//\n// prd002-sys R2.3.\nfunc fillFromStat(fi *FileInfo, st *unix.Stat_t) {\n\tfi.ModTime = time.Unix(st.Mtim.Sec, st.Mtim.Nsec)\n\tfi.Nlink = uint64(st.Nlink)\n\tfi.Dev = st.Dev\n\tfi.Rdev = st.Rdev\n\tfi.Blksize = int64(st.Blksize)\n}\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}}}
